1431 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 797 0 R
/T (The Problem: Every screen on a mobile app is just a giant Composite tree of UI elements \(a Screen contains a ScrollView, which contains Buttons, TextViews, and Images\). How to traverse through all of these to change theme?)
/E (The Problem: Every screen on a mobile app is just a giant Composite tree of UI elements \(a Screen contains a ScrollView, which contains Buttons, TextViews, and Images\). How to traverse through all of these to change theme?)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1432 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 797 0 R
/T (The Visitor Solution: You implement a ThemeVisitor. You pass it to the root of the screen, and it recursively visits every child element. When it visits a TextView, it changes the font color to white. When it visits a View background, it changes it to dark gray. The UI elements just accept the visitor without caring about the theme logic.)
/E (The Visitor Solution: You implement a ThemeVisitor. You pass it to the root of the screen, and it recursively visits every child element. When it visits a TextView, it changes the font color to white. When it visits a View background, it changes it to dark gray. The UI elements just accept the visitor without caring about the theme logic.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
